Wolf3D x64 @PROJECT_VERSION@ (preview)
==============================

A faithful port of id Software's Wolfenstein 3-D (1992) to 64-bit Windows
and Linux: the original engine, AI, screens and control panel, the AdLib
music and the Sound Blaster effects, with mouse, game pad and scalable
windows added. Free software under the GPL-2.0 (LICENSE.txt).

This is a preview: everything is in, and the first players are the
playtest. Found something? https://github.com/mkalkhoven-po/wolf3d-x64/issues


What you need: your own game files
----------------------------------

This package holds the game program only, no game data. Use your own
Wolfenstein 3-D files, version 1.4:

  - the shareware (episode 1): the files end in .WL1
  - the full version (all six episodes): the files end in .WL6
    (the copies sold today, for instance on Steam or GOG, are this one)

The files needed: VSWAP, VGAGRAPH, VGAHEAD, VGADICT, GAMEMAPS, MAPHEAD,
AUDIOHED and AUDIOT, each ending in .WL1 or .WL6.


Starting
--------

Easiest: copy those files into the "data" folder next to the game, then
start the game. Or start it anywhere: when it finds no game files it asks
for the folder they are in, and remembers it.

Windows: double-click wolf3d.exe. Windows may say "Windows protected your
PC", because the program is new and not signed: choose "More info", then
"Run anyway". SDL2.dll must stay next to wolf3d.exe.

Linux: run ./wolf3d. It needs SDL2 (Debian / Ubuntu: sudo apt install
libsdl2-2.0-0; Fedora: sudo dnf install SDL2). Asking for the folder
needs zenity or kdialog; without them, start it as
./wolf3d --data /path/to/your/files


Playing
-------

As in the original: any key on the title pages opens the control panel,
New Game starts. Esc in the game opens the control panel again. The
original keys (arrows, Ctrl shoots, Space opens doors, Alt strafes,
Shift runs, 1-4 pick a weapon); F11 switches fullscreen. Mouse: turn on
Mouse Enabled in the Control menu. Game pad (Xbox, PlayStation and
others): left stick walks, right stick turns, RT or A shoots, X opens
doors, Start is Esc. The Sound, Video and Control menus hold the
settings.


Where your settings and saves are
---------------------------------

Windows: %APPDATA%\Wolf3D-x64\
Linux:   ~/.local/share/Wolf3D-x64/

config.ini (settings), the high scores, the ten save slots of each
version, and on Windows wolf3d.log (what the last start printed; please
add it to a bug report).


